@startuml authentication-lockout-sequence
' Status: Draft - Reconciliation Incomplete. AI-reconciled; not human reviewed (Principle VII).
' Written source: contracts/service-contracts.md, DEC-23
title Authentication and Lockout\nFR-002, FR-004, NFR-002 (conditional draft: OC-1 open)

actor "Visitor" as Visitor
participant "LoginPanel" as Panel
participant "SessionController\n(via UiTaskRunner)" as Ctrl
participant "AccountService" as Svc
participant "TransactionRunner" as Tx
database "UserRepository" as Repo
participant "User" as UserEntity
participant "PasswordHasher" as Hasher
participant "Clock" as Clock

Visitor -> Panel : username, password
Panel -> Ctrl : submit; password field cleared
Ctrl -> Svc : login(LoginCommand)
Svc -> Clock : now
Svc -> Tx : readOnly
Tx -> Repo : findByUsernameKey(key)
Repo --> Svc : user or empty

alt unknown username
  Svc -> Hasher : verify(password, dummy hash)
  note right of Hasher : Limits timing differences.
  Svc --> Ctrl : AuthenticationFailedException
  Ctrl --> Panel : one generic message
else account is locked: now before lockedUntil
  note right of Svc
    Refused before any password check.
    The attempt neither counts nor extends the lock.
    Revealing "locked" is an accepted trade-off (DEC-23).
  end note
  Svc --> Ctrl : AccountLockedException(lockedUntil)
  Ctrl --> Panel : "temporarily locked"
else not locked
  Svc -> Hasher : verify(password, passwordHash)
  note right of Hasher : Slow; runs outside any transaction.\nConstant-time comparison.
  alt wrong password
    Hasher --> Svc : false
    Svc -> UserEntity : recordFailedLogin(now)
    note right of UserEntity : A lock that has expired restarts the count.\nFifth failure: lockedUntil = now + 5 minutes.
    Svc -> Tx : inTransaction
    activate Tx
    Tx -> Repo : updateLoginState(id, count, lockedUntil)
    Tx --> Svc : **commit first**
    deactivate Tx
    note right of Svc : Raising inside the transaction would roll back\nthe count and disable lockout.
    Svc --> Ctrl : AuthenticationFailedException
    Ctrl --> Panel : one generic message
  else correct password
    Hasher --> Svc : true
    Svc -> UserEntity : recordSuccessfulLogin()
    Svc -> Tx : inTransaction
    activate Tx
    Tx -> Repo : updateLoginState(id, 0, none)
    Tx --> Svc : commit
    deactivate Tx
    Svc --> Ctrl : Session
    Ctrl --> Panel : open Home with unread count
  end
end

== Log out (FR-002) ==
Visitor -> Ctrl : Log Out
Ctrl -> Svc : logout(session)
Svc -> Svc : invalidate session
Ctrl --> Panel : dispose user views; show Login
note right of Ctrl : UiTaskRunner drops any late result\nfrom the ended session.

@enduml
